**B1.** The parts below are stored verbatim in `session-tools/b846/texts.py` (extracted by markers from your Step-0 copy, each asserted to occur once; sha256 of each in STATUS), assembled into ADF with the project's own `jira-adf.py` (copy `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/b788/jira-adf.py`, expected sha256 `1e64c64c9f05c20ff7847ca0669e6a60ea23ba3d8f41d6f79398c546397e72ac`, `shasum` it; its `doc()` validates before any request): `h("BLUF")`, `p(t(BLUF))`, `h("Recommendation")`, `p(t(REC))`, `h("Detail")`, `bl([...])`. Copy `session-tools/b788/b788lib.py` (sha256 `b533c5fb085a417d71f19c50f6a945c6838884e5716ac537b0e7dbebc55375d7`) and keep ONLY `get`, `search`, `comments`, `issue`, `adf_texts`, `post_comment`, `create`, `transitions` (GET); replace its `do_transition` with `do_testing(key)`, which re-GETs `transitions`, picks the entry whose `name` is "In Review" AND `to.name` is "Testing" (refuse on none or two), POSTs that id once, and never uses a literal id or the id 51 or 101. **Substitutions (the only ones):** `{READ-TIME}` = `HH:MM` AEDT from your own `date` at A1; `{DEMO-RUNS}` = the A1d count; `{T1}`, `{T2}`, `{T3}` = the keys of the three tickets (created or found in Job C1, before the comments are assembled); `{ALERT-LINE-873}` and `{ALERT-LINE-811}` built from A1b in this exact format, one item per alert in the order given, joined by "; ": `<n> fixed (fixed_at YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM AEDT)` or `<n> open` (873 order: 274, 116, 97, 234, 238, 96, 98, 99, 95; 811 order: 234, 238). **Branch rule:** RD-873 uses the `-A` BLUF and REC when alerts 96, 97, 98, 99 and 116 ALL read fixed, else the `-B` pair; RD-811 uses `-A` when 234 and 238 both read fixed, else `-B`. The unused branch is never posted.
**Per-figure assert (before assembly, by program).** For every assembled text: extract each digit-bearing token (shas, run ids, counts, line numbers, times, PR and alert numbers) and require that it is present in a named A1/A1b/A1c/A1d/A1e/A2 read (or, for gate figures, in the quoted gate line it is RELAYED from: `B827_STATUS.md`, `B838_STATUS.md`, `B837_STATUS.md`, re-read for this); an unmatched token HOLDS that key and goes to FOR TUESDAY with the token. Fixed checks at least these: every merge sha, parent, head, tree and `merged_at` (as AEDT), file path with its +/-; the run ids and conclusions of the twelve push runs; the counts pairs; the 2026-10-27 times of the attempts (13:45-14:37, 15:15-16:00 AEDT) from `run_started_at` and `updated_at`; the alert states in the `-A` branch; "0 open" on the PR-ref twins; the `{DEMO-RUNS}` equalities; every `{...}` consumed (no brace left in any text; control: a planted brace is refused). Skip markers (a comment already containing it SKIPS the key; a summary that already exists SKIPS the create): RD-891 `merge commit c8e1a9a1`; RD-873 `merge commit 0de3eb2f`; RD-811 `merge commit 0de3eb2f`; RD-893 `merge commit f61de45f`; RD-884 `registry build of the current Dockerfile`; RD-757 `cell B4`. Each text starts with BLUF, has the three headings in order, passes the scans.

## JOB C · CREATE, THEN POST (A and B must have ended in their part lines)
**C1. The three tickets, in order T1, T2, T3.** First `search` by the exact summary (a case-sensitive equality on the returned summaries; expect 0); a hit SKIPS the create and the existing key is used. Create with `create(fields)`, ONE attempt, timeout 60 s: `project` RD, `issuetype` Task, `summary` (<= 255 characters, asserted), `description` the ADF of `h("BLUF")`, `p(t(BLUF))`, `h("Recommendation")`, `p(t(REC))`, `h("Detail")`, `bl([...])`, `priority` Low, `labels` as the part says plus `b846-2026-10-27`; no parent, no component, no link (the shape of RD-891, RD-892 and RD-893). On a timeout or error never repeat blindly: search by the summary and repeat only if it is still absent, once. Read back by key: summary equal to what was sent, status To Do, `adf_texts` of the description equal to what was sent (a one-character mutant compares unequal). A failed create is a STOP (comments cite the keys). Part line: `JOB C1: <n> tickets (T1=<key>, T2=<key>, T3=<key>), SKIPS <...>`.
**C2. The six comments.** Per key in the order RD-891, RD-873, RD-811, RD-893, RD-884, RD-757: re-GET status and count immediately before; `POST /rest/api/3/issue/<key>/comment`, timeout 60 s, ONE attempt; on a timeout or error never repeat blindly: GET the list and repeat only if the count is unchanged, once. Read back by id: `adf_texts` equal to what was sent (a one-character mutant compares unequal); count exactly +1; status unchanged. Quote key, comment id, count before and after, status after. Part line: `JOB C2: <n> comments (RD-891=<id>, ...), SKIPS <...>, HELD <...>`.

## JOB D · THE TESTING MOVES (only after the key's own comment is read back, and only where the move rule is met)
**D1.** In this order: **RD-891** if its comment was posted or SKIPPED-because-present, status still To Do, and Build 40454239092 read success at A1; **RD-873** if `-A` was used, both Builds (40474611793 and 40474686389) read success, status still To Do; **RD-811** if `-A` was used, both Builds read success, status still To Do. RD-893, RD-884 and RD-757 are never moved. For each: `do_testing(key)` (one POST), then GET: status must read `Testing`; any other status (`Declined` above all) is a STOP with the key and id quoted. Control: your assertion refuses a planted `Declined`, a planted list with two "In Review" entries, and a planted list whose "In Review" lands on `Done`. Part line: `JOB D: <key> transition <id> by name In Review, status after <s>` per key; a key whose comment was HELD or whose condition failed: no transition, say why.

